---
/*
 * [WEB-REPOSITION-2 2026-08-28] Rewritten from "Your AI brain, in every chat",
 * which sold the in-chat Ava assistant — a feature the 2026-08-27 pivot is
 * taking DARK. Leaving it published would have advertised something we are
 * switching off. The URL is kept alive rather than 404'd.
 *
 * Replaced with the question a new creator actually has: what do I charge.
 * Deliberately NO invented numbers — the commission rate and any payout minimum
 * are "shown before you commit" per /pricing-fees and /payouts, and a blog post
 * must not contradict the policy pages. 100 Tokens = $1 is the internal anchor,
 * so that one is safe to state.
 */
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../../layouts/Content.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Blog · Getting started"
  title="How to price your first listing"
  description="A practical guide to setting your price on avaTOK — how tokens work, what to charge for a first session, and how the money reaches your bank."
  lead="100 Tokens = $1 internally. Beyond that, the number is yours to choose — here is how to choose it."
  updated="2026-08-28"
>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.77bfb7330eee5178">
    Most people setting a price for the first time do the same two things: they guess, and they
    guess low. It is worth a few minutes of thought instead, because the number you publish is the
    single biggest lever on whether this is worth your evening.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.475071a2edb84069">First, the unit</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.911bdefe76ecebc3">avaTOK prices everything in</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-blog.c51e455b41df6c01">tokens</strong><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.5dc7680cacec826b">, with</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-blog.1333886bf7b67378">100 Tokens = $1</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.c31144cd12725a30">as the
    rate is fixed, both directions — it is what a customer pays to buy tokens, and what an unused
    token is worth on the way out. Checkout may be shown in local currency using a server-owned FX
    quote; there is no promised withdrawal or redemption rate. Full detail is in</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.188dc350278985ab" href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.7aa027b7698b4c40">Price the outcome, not the minutes</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.4e0bb30dd3f1fc5c">
    "X tokens per hour" is the instinctive framing, and it is usually the weakest one. People are not
    buying an hour; they are buying the thing that is true afterwards — the doubt resolved, the
    thing they finally understand, the evening they did not spend alone. A session that gets someone
    there in twenty minutes is worth more to them than one that takes ninety, not less.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.c90ca18d174ac68b">Start where you can raise it</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.13aa33070253bd45">
    Set a price you would be content to be booked at ten times this month, then raise it when you
    are. Raising a price on a listing that is filling up is easy and nobody resents it. Cutting a
    price you announced too confidently is harder, and it teaches the people who already paid that
    they overpaid.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.f8cbe6c121ab0a84">Know what you actually keep</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.4ba82a9aea8c4bfb">The customer pays your listed price. avaTOK deducts a platform commission, which is shown to you
    before you publish a listing or accept a booking — we do not spring it on you afterwards. What
    remains is credited to your wallet in tokens. Withdrawal semantics are not yet available, so no
    payout fee, tax, minimum, or timeline is promised.
    See</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-blog.5e2a4b33bff1936b" href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.6201111b83a0cb5b">and</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.aba115e7791e41dc" href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.e007d3ad4688c558">for the rules in full.</ui-copy>
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.278dd8f6849d150b">Then get the calendar right</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.aa9313237f2ff3ad">A good price on hours you resent is still a bad deal. Open the slots you actually want to work —
    see</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-blog.eb471b2ca49cb5e8" href="/blog/never-miss-a-call">how bookings work</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong data-i18n="web-blog.e424a72c45ead7d6">avaTOK is still evolving.</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.1b2cff25f07a7568">We are an early-stage Delaware corporation,
      business, access is invite-only, and our payment gateway application is under review,
      so payments are not yet live to the public. Prices shown on the site are indicative during
      this period.</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-blog.1e7c107176e052c9" href="/terms#status">Read our full status</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.cd080826543612ac" href="/sign-up">Publish your first listing</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.f3c3a1f016a07e56">— it is free — or</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.41a8f9b7bbd48e29" href="/marketplace">see how other creators have priced theirs</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
